#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0061 expect=noViolation domain=AE
#note "The Define-XML sidecar declares AE and DM (both present in the study) plus a third ItemGroupDef WITHOUT a Name. A nameless ItemGroupDef names no dataset, so the Define provider skips it (register NNL 1) and define_dataset_names() is exactly [AE, DM] -> contains_all holds -> no violation. Before the fix the nameless entry entered the list as a null, folded to the empty name, and the rule fired with $missing_datasets = []."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#define-xml PMDA-SD0061-nameless-define.xml
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE
---

dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | DM | 001
